<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="GBrowser: What's new" id="GBrowser-Whats-New">

    <primary-label ref="gbrowser"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Current version: 2026.3.1, for JetBrains IDEs 2026.3 (EAP builds 263.3889 and later)</p>
        <p>For JetBrains IDEs 2026.2: GBrowser 2026.2.3</p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Release notes for GBrowser: IDE support, device emulation, page theme, browser compatibility mode and fixes.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Release notes for recent GBrowser versions.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>What's new in GBrowser for JetBrains IDEs: support for 2026.3, device emulation, page theme, Open in GBrowser and browser compatibility mode.</web-summary>

    <p>
        This page lists the changes in recent GBrowser releases, newest first.
        For every release, see the <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/GBrowser/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">changelog on GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <chapter title="2026.3" id="v2026-3">
        <p><b>2026.3.1</b>, September 5, 2026:</p>
        <list>
            <li>Support for the 2026.3 EAP of JetBrains IDEs (build 263.3889 and later 263 builds).</li>
            <li>Updated dependencies.</li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.2" id="v2026-2">
        <p><b>2026.2.3</b>, July 19, 2026:</p>
        <list>
            <li>Updated dependencies.</li>
        </list>
        <p><b>2026.2.1</b>, June 13, 2026:</p>
        <list>
            <li>Support for JetBrains IDEs 2026.2.</li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.1" id="v2026-1">
        <p><b>2026.1.7</b> and <b>2026.1.8</b>, April 11 and May 1, 2026:</p>
        <list>
            <li>Platform and dependency updates.</li>
        </list>
        <p><b>2026.1.6</b>, April 8, 2026:</p>
        <list>
            <li>Fixed an IDE error ("Access is allowed from Event Dispatch Thread (EDT) only") that GBrowser could cause.</li>
        </list>
        <p><b>2026.1.3</b> to <b>2026.1.5</b>, March 2026:</p>
        <list>
            <li>Platform and dependency updates.</li>
        </list>
        <p><b>2026.1.1</b> and <b>2026.1.2</b>, January 23 and 24, 2026:</p>
        <list>
            <li>Support for JetBrains IDEs 2026.1.</li>
            <li>The <control>Enable drag and drop tabs</control> setting is now named <control>Enable tab splitting</control>.</li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2025.3" id="v2025-3">
        <p><b>2025.3.7</b>, November 6, 2025:</p>
        <list>
            <li>Fixed an error about a component that must be shown on the screen.</li>
            <li>Fixed invalid HTML on the page that GBrowser shows when a page cannot be loaded.</li>
            <li>Fixed an empty menu item text for <control>Open Selected Text in GBrowser</control>.</li>
        </list>
        <p><b>2025.3.1</b>, September 18, 2025:</p>
        <list>
            <li>
                <a href="GBrowser-Settings-and-Configuration.topic" anchor="browser-compatibility-mode">Browser compatibility mode</a>
                helps with sites that block embedded browsers, with a list of compatible sites in the settings.
            </li>
            <li>
                <control>Open DevTools</control> now opens Chromium DevTools in a separate window.
                The DevTools tool window is no longer available.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2025.2" id="v2025-2">
        <p><b>2025.2.3</b>, July 26, 2025:</p>
        <list>
            <li>
                <a href="GBrowser-DevTools-and-Device-Emulation.topic" anchor="device-emulation">Device emulation</a>:
                show pages at the screen size of phones and tablets.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="GBrowser-Settings-and-Configuration.topic" anchor="appearance">Page theme</a>:
                pages can follow the IDE theme or use a light or dark color scheme.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="GBrowser-Open-Files-and-Links.topic"/>: the <control>Open in GBrowser</control> action opens HTML, SVG and other files from your project.
            </li>
            <li>Support for JetBrains IDEs 2025.2.</li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

